### Calls for the demo server. In IntelliJ IDEA (HTTP Client) or VS Code (REST Client extension) click "Send Request" above each block.
### Start the server first:  ./serve.sh

### 1. List books, 2 per page (query parameters -> @RequestParam)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books?page=0&size=2

### 2. One book (path segment -> @PathVariable)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books/1

### 3. Unknown id -> 404 problem detail (BookNotFoundException -> GlobalExceptionHandler)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books/999

### 4. Search by author (derived query: findByAuthorIgnoreCase)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books/search?author=george orwell

### 5. Search by title (hand-written @Query)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books/search?title=ring

### 6. Cheaper than 10 (derived query: findByPriceLessThanEqualOrderByPrice)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books/search?maxPrice=10

### 7. Create a book -> 201 Created + Location header
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Clean Code", "author": "Robert C. Martin", "price": 33.50}

### 8. Invalid body -> 400 with the list of bad fields (@Valid)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "", "author": "X", "price": -1}

### 9. Update
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/books/1
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Nineteen Eighty-Four", "author": "George Orwell", "price": 10.50}

### 10. Delete -> 204 No Content
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/books/6

### 11. Discount 50 percent: the UPDATE is issued by dirty checking, there is no save() call. Watch the SQL in the console.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books/5/discount?percent=50

### 12. Discount outside 1..90 -> 400
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books/5/discount?percent=95

### 13. Transaction ROLLBACK: the first book is saved, then an exception is thrown; neither book is stored. Compare GET /api/books before and after.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books/batch?failAfterFirst=true
Content-Type: application/json

[{"title": "A", "author": "A", "price": 1}, {"title": "B", "author": "B", "price": 2}]

### 14. Same batch without the failure: both are stored
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books/batch
Content-Type: application/json

[{"title": "A", "author": "A", "price": 1}, {"title": "B", "author": "B", "price": 2}]

### 15. Configuration: values from application.yml, active profile, @Value default
GET http://localhost:8080/api/hello

### 16. The journey of a request: Filter -> Interceptor -> Controller -> AOP (same lines in the console)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/debug/flow

### 16b. The REAL call stack from Tomcat down to the controller method
GET http://localhost:8080/api/debug/stack

### 17. The injected beans are generated proxies, not your classes
GET http://localhost:8080/api/debug/proxies

### 18. Actuator: look inside the running application
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/health

###
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/beans

###
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/mappings

###
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/env

### 19. Wrong HTTP method -> 405, wrong content type -> 415 (default handling of Spring MVC's own exceptions)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/books

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books
Content-Type: text/plain

hello
